Z||000014||California Kid||11-03-2001||03:19 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by WKDFIRO:<BR><B>Has the engine been worked on since it arrived in Michigan other than the paint, intake mods and shiney things put on?<P>I still think it was a better sleeper when it was black, but it does look good in yellow! Congrats! <P>A build up article of that car was in Kit Car magazine (Keith still has the issue) as well. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Mild port work to the heads, lower intake, plenum opened up, port matched to SLP runner, and twin 52mm throttle body (it's asking for a 58mm). Ignition modified with HP distributor module and MSD unit. Adjustable fuel pressure regulator and high flow fuel pump, plus some other minor stuff to improve performance.<P>Thanks!  If you see Keith, tell him the car is taking plenty of trophies at hot rod shows, know he will appreciate that.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by California Kid (edited 11-03-2001).]||||reg||1
